      "trace_id": "cd2dedc788e9c0f4700801f18d0532ec",
      "output": {
        "question": "what is the sumary of the first book?",
        "answer": "Mikael Blomkvist investigates what happened to Harriet Vanger, whose disappearance has haunted her family for decades; the job also offers him information about Wennerström [E1]. With Lisbeth Salander’s help, he uncovers that Martin Vanger was a serial killer, and that Harriet had killed her father and fled her brother; she eventually built a new life in Australia [E2] [E3] [E4].",
        "citations": [
          "[E1]",
          "[E2]",
          "[E3]",
          "[E4]"
        ],
        "reranked": [
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_017.html",
            "paragraph": 79,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 9 Monday, January 6– Wednesday, January 8",
            "page": "16",
            "text": "Blomkvist had had to remind himself several times that his real assignment was not to write a biography of the Vanger family but to find out what had happened to Harriet Vanger. The Vanger biography would be no more than playing to the gallery. After a year he would receive his preposterous salary—the contract drawn up by Frode had been signed. His true reward, he hoped, would be the information about Wennerström that Vanger claimed to possess. But after listening to Vanger, he began to see that the year did not have to be a waste of time. A book about the Vanger family had significant value. It was, quite simply, a terrific story.",
            "paragraph_end": 79,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "089cc6d3a4667b2cc92cc0c5b9228f50500c00ba3a61d8aff559ea3deac366df",
            "id": "089cc6d3-a466-7b2c-c92c-c0c5b9228f50",
            "keyword_score": 19.713032524063713,
            "score": 19.713032524063713,
            "agent_label": "E1"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_035.html",
            "paragraph": 38,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 25 Saturday, July 12– Monday, July 14",
            "page": "34",
            "text": "Frode gave her a searching look.\n“I don’t understand.”\n“You don’t need to understand.”\n“Then what should I do?”\n“You’ll have to work that out for yourself. Only leave me and Mikael out of it.”\nFrode was deathly pale.\n“Look at it this way: the only thing you know is that Martin Vanger died in a traffic accident. You have no idea that he was also an insane, nauseating serial killer, and you’ve never heard about the room in his basement.”",
            "paragraph_end": 44,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "1c3a48ac435aa1bbbb6206021082861e85bc9b44f960b908d4a8f1a8115d5101",
            "id": "1c3a48ac-435a-a1bb-bb62-06021082861e",
            "agent_label": "E2"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_035.html",
            "paragraph": 134,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 25 Saturday, July 12– Monday, July 14",
            "page": "34",
            "text": "“It was Martin,” Salander said. “Her father was dead, but Martin was going on abusing her.”\n“Exactly.”\n“But it was a year before she took any action.”\n“What would you do if you found out that your father was a murderer who had been raping your brother?”\n“I’d kill the fucker,” Salander said in such a sober tone that Blomkvist believed her. He remembered her face as she was attacking Martin Vanger. He smiled joylessly.",
            "paragraph_end": 138,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "989132635ccb8d61137ccb41ab274fcc36e7164d5213ad0dd81df194c1993345",
            "id": "98913263-5ccb-8d61-137c-cb41ab274fcc",
            "agent_label": "E3"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Played with Fire",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Played with Fire _ A Lisbeth Salander Novel -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium trilogy, bk_ 2, New York, 2009 -- Alfred A_ Knopf -- isbn13 9780307272300 -- 078fc916144df1e3707c069bbf984d06 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_who-ayed_with_Fire_split_018.html",
            "paragraph": 137,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": null,
            "page": "32",
            "text": "She had had sex with three men in her life. First her father and then her brother. She had killed her father and run away from her brother. Somehow she had survived and met a man with whom she had created a new life for herself.\n“He was tender and loving. Dependable and honest. I was happy with him. We had a wonderful twenty years together before he became ill.”\n“You never remarried? Why not?”\nShe shrugged. “I was the mother of two children in Australia and the owner of a big agricultural business. I could never get away for a romantic weekend. And I’ve never missed sex.” They sat quiet for a while. “It’s late. I should be getting back to the hotel.”",
            "paragraph_end": 140,
            "part_end": 1,
